    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Okay, so my impression is this: This looks most like alcohol withdrawal. Another possibility is an anxiety state.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:07",
      "end_timestamp": "04:15",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_assessment[0]",
        "clinical_assessment[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's alcohol withdrawal, and we'll know more once the blood tests is back. I'd like to arrange blood tests for alcohol withdrawal. For this, chlordiazepoxide, 20 milligrams, four times a day, reducing over five days. That's for alcohol withdrawal. The treatment will be thiamine, 100 milligrams, three times a day, long term. It's for alcohol-related deficiency. Do not stop alcohol suddenly without medical support.",
